Package: bbq
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Bi-Aspect Quantile Change-Point Detection
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Yuhui", "Yao",
      email = "yyao17@ua.edu",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Retrospective (Phase I) change-point detection for individual
    autocorrelated observations without distributional assumptions. Three
    quantile levels are modeled jointly by Bayesian multiple quantile regression
    with a score likelihood, non-crossing and interquantile penalties, and
    sparsity-inducing priors on block shift coefficients, fitted by maximum a
    posteriori estimation with a Laplace approximation via 'Stan'. Decorrelated
    union-intersection statistics identify shifted blocks on the quantile basis
    and on the location (median) and scale (interquartile range) basis.
